{\qc
168: Chapter 167\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So{\b
 yeah, it's been a real long ass time since I uploaded on here. Honestly, I just kind of forgot to upload here? Sorry about that. My life has just been pretty hectic. I haven't stopped writing at all mind you, slowed down a little but, but picked up again in speed recently. And if you wanna read advanced chapters, you can check them out on my Subscribestar, same name I use on here,- 0Jordinio0}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Also wanna thank you guys who got in contact with me about the dudes who keep plagarising my stories, like that one dude who keeps re-uploading To Go Even Further Beyond every time he gets reported and the story taken down.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
_______________________}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He landed before Pidgeot, Togepi and I moments later, his new\u8230?friends? Landing beside him a few seconds later.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looking at him beside them all, he positively towered over them. He had practically twice the mass of any of the other Fearow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Yeah, that's my try hard bird!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Make some new friends mate?" I grinned at him, raising an eyebrow. Does he want me to catch them?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I'd planned on slowing down on that kind of thing, catching big groups of the same pokemon like a collector ever since I had my epiphany with Surge. But, if Fearow wanted to bring his friends along and they were in agreement, then I would.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fearow being happy is more important after all than me being a better person.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Feeeerow!" he puffed his chest out.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Looking them over, there were eleven in total not counting my Fearow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Any luck?" I asked Fearow, though my hopes for Tyranitar were already rock bottom.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No matter. It wasn't that big of a deal I suppose.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Row row Fearow row!" Fearow shook his head and barked back, before gesturing to his new buddies, "Row row fee!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fearow claims he had no luck finding the Tyranitar you seek," Rotom offered from my hand, almost making me jump in surprise, my eyes widening, how could I forget Rotom is a pokemon and could understand them. And can now translate for me! "But as he was searching he came across this flock of Fearow and sought information on Tyranitar's where abouts. They refused to give out such information and came to blows, Fearow quickly defeating the leader of the flock\u8230?and now they have bowed to Fearow as their new leader."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Huh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It hasn't even been a half an hour and my Fearow had literally taken over another flock casually while searching for something for me.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That's one of my try hards for you. Being an epic try hard even when not meaning to.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I shook my head, "So you want to bring them along then?" I asked Fearow, looking them over.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
While they weren't as big as my Fearow, they weren't exactly small little things either. And there weren't any Spearow among them. I'm not exactly sure why.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They could be useful I suppose. A team of flying bird scouts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fearow row row." Fearow sighed, before shrugging his wings and nodding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fearow claims that while it wasn't his intention at first, he has to take responsibility for accepting the battle in the first place," Rotom relayed, "Though if you do not want to bring them along, he will send them away."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I rolled my eyes, "Nah if you want to take responsibility, I'll catch them," I shrugged, again Fearow's happiness is important. It sure is hard trying to be a better person, "Though they won't be able to come along with us, you'll be able to see them when we visit, more so when our new home is built."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Fearow nodded, before looking over at the assembled flock of Fearow and barking out a few things at them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And then they began giving crowing cheers from their long beaks, wings raised in celebration.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Huh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I guess they really like Fearow?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I sighed, "It's too bad about Tyranitar I suppose."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As I said that, Fearow turned back to me and blinked, before his eyes widened and he began to wave his wings frantically, "Row row fearow fearow row!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A frantic apology?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Really, there's no need to feel that bad about not finding Tyranitar and getting caught up with-\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fearow apologises for not stating so sooner, but he demanded all the flock of Fearow knew about the Tyranitar you seek before accepting his place as the leader of the flock," Rotom cut his thoughts off, "He has already found where the Tyranitar is nesting."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230?Oh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Huh.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I grinned, hopping off Pidgeot's back, and holding Togepi in one arm I wrapped Fearow in a big hug, "Well done mate!" I laughed, "Look at you go, taking over another group of Fearow and finding Tyranitar at the same time! you're amazing mate!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Row!" Fearow beamed joyfully.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Geot!" Pidgeot huffed, rolling his eyes and flicked his long mane of hair back.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
_________________\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As it turned out, Tyranitar had taken up residence in a cave on the opposite side of the valley from the ancient ruin where Regice resided.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Whether that was intentional or not to avoid the legendary pokemon I couldn't say.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nor did it really matter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After catching the flock of eleven Fearow and returning\u8230?Fearow. I hopped back up on Pidgeots back and we made our way over to where my new flock had told me where Tyranitar resided.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And it wasn't long before we found it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was truly massive. A towering behemoth well over ten feet tall, made up of purely muscled rocky plate that was lounging over a massive boulder lazily, directly until the suns warm rays.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It narrowed its eyes at me and Pidgeot as we landed a good ten feet away, but didn't tense up at all. It didn't feel threatened at all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As expected of a Pseudo Legendary.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tyranitar," I pointed to it with a grin in greeting, "I've come to catch you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I'd already recalled Togepi for now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Tyranitar scoffed as it pushed itself up off the rock it was tanning on, rolling its slitted eyes at me and Pidgeot.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This is a good time for one of my pokemon to make their first official battle debut and not just training battles with my other pokemon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I pressed a few buttons on the back of my Rotom Gauntlet and a moment later, a gleaming ebony black luxury ball deposited into my hand from the gauntlet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Let's go, Blastoise!" I said, releasing the pokemon from within the luxury ball in a burst of bright light.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
