179: Chapter 178\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
If you wanna read ahead of my stories, you can check out the advanced chapters on my subcribestar, at the same username - 0Jordinio0}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Just about caught up everything I have for Systematic Shinobi for the moment, so will be actively uploading what I have for this now.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
_____________}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It didn't take all that long, even with Aerodactyl's slower flight speed to reach our destination.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not far from Pewter City, Aerodactyl touched down in front of a massive mausoleum. It was a near perfect replica of the one he saw in Fennel Valley, only this one was deep within the Viridian Forest. Trees and Foliage had grown wild around it, blotting it almost from view.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The home of Regirock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Or\u8230?more like prison really.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As soon as I landed on Aerodactyl's massive form, dozens of pokemon roosting or lounging in the area made a break for it into the deeper forest. Mostly a bunch of caterpie, but a few pidgey in the trees followed suit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good work mate." I returned Aerodactyl to his ball after I stepped off of his back, storing it back inside my gauntlet before making my way inside the huge abandoned ruin.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Even the inside was identical to the one if Fennel Valley. Right up into the main chamber containing a replica of that ugly ass statue of the evil bastard king, throne and all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Luckily, I already had the other throne so I didn't need to bother with that this time around.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230?Not that I should have in the first place, but god it was just so gaudy I couldn't help myself.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Shaking my head, I looked away, my gaze zeroing in on the puzzle on the wall to the far side of the massive main chamber.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8230?Now how to go about this?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All out water offensive? I could lead with both Gyarados and Blastoise, smashing Regirock with Hydro Pump before it even wakes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But no, super effective or not, it would just shake it easily because of the sheer gulf in power between them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I suppose I'll just rout it the same way I did Regice, but with both Exeggutor and Golem at the same time. Laying it flat with the explosions and status effects were the way to go.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They'd both already fought today, but I'd had them healed up by Blissey. Still, they'd expanded a lot of energy against Regice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So after I take care of Regirock, I'll call it a night and let them rest for the night, and leave Registeel until tomorrow morning.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I could most likely do it without Exeggutor and Golem, especially with Regice on my side now, but setting up with the two of them, would make it much easier to bring them down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A normal full on battle would most likely bring down the Mausoleum down on top of my head, destroying the ancient building in total.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With that thought in mind, I grabbed both of their gleaming black luxurious luxury balls from my gauntlet storage, and released them both.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Both appeared in bursts of silver light beside me, "Same as before you two," I told them, "Only this time, at the same time."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Exeggutor gave a sleepy trio of murmurs and nods, while Golem grinned and flashed me a thumbs up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I pointed at the wall, "Break this one down as well with Brick Break, Golem." I ordered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gol!" he nodded and walked forward, both myself and Exeggutor trailing behind him as he wound up his arm, now glowing with power and ploughed straight through the puzzle wall, as he had done earlier with the first one.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Smoke and debris wafted around us as we stepped into the chamber containing Regirock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Like the one from earlier, it was empty save for a towering plateau of stairs rising high up above us, into a wide platform where the slumbering form of Regirock waited, alongside another large treasure chest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I watched as its orange eyes flickered with golden light, "Un!\u8230?Un!\u8230?Un!" its slumped over form straightened up as it began awakening.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exeggutor go! Middle Leech Seed, Left, Sleep Powder, Right Poison Powder!" I commanded, lifting my gauntlet clad fist, "Golem, Sand Attack its eyes, blind it! Rotom, Thunder Wave!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
My pokemon leapt into action. The second the commands left my mouth, they burst forth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
From the left and right heads of Exeggutor, huge clouds of spores erupted from their mouths, glittering spores of cyan blue and deep royal purple. At the same time, Golem roared and tore one of his arms through the ground and tossed forth a literal wave of sand up amongst them, creating a crescent over Regirock's massive rocky form that cast a shadow upon it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the same time the middle spat forth a seed like a bullet, it pierced through the spores and sand both hitting the legendary rock type square in the face, before exploding into thick vines that wrapped tightly around Regirock's body, lighting up its body in shocks of crimson red that began to rapidly sap its energy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Un!" It made to spread its massive thick powerful rock arms out and tear the vines from its body, but before it could the amalgamation of spores and sand washed over its body,\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sand caked it from head to toe, covering its face, at the same time it slumped over falling asleep once more and its body bubbled with a venomous purple glow as poison took root.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And to hammer it in, a thin bolt of blue electricity erupted from my gauntlet clad palm, striking the now sleeping Regirock, paralyzing it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Asleep, paralyzed, poisoned, eyes covered in sand and its energy now being rapidly drained by Leech Seed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
All before it even barely got the chance to really wake up and see what the hell was going on.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I am such a bad guy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You know what to do!" I continued, winding my fist back, even as I stepped back out of the room, taking cover behind the walls "Both of you, Explosion!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Golem!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exeggutor!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With cries of affirmation, both of them rushed forward and up the winding plateau of stairs, bodies beginning to glow a bright white with trembling crackling power.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And a second later, my vision went white as they erupted in twin thunderous explosions as soon as they reached the top and got beside Regirock, even hidden behind the walls as I was, and my hearing was drowned out as the world thundered and shook around me, the entire mausoleum shaking as if it were going to fall apart from the explosive force.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
_____________\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Rosa linked her fingers together and chuckled ominiously within a dark shadowy room, the only light, casting on her face, illuminated by the moonlight streaming in from the secure window, where none would see, "All according to cake, kukukukuku!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
Then a thump on the door made her yelp and jump.}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
{\b
"Rosa will you get out of the bathroom already!" Hilda huffed from outside, "You've been in there making weird giggles for an hour already, you better not be masturbating again!"}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
